--- SURFACE NOTES: AdvancedSettings (parity port of web/src/features/settings/components/AdvancedSettings.tsx) ---
- The web component is the "Restore confirmation prompts" panel: it reads the silenced confirm-dialog ids
  synchronously from local storage (listSilenced/unsilence/clearAllSilenced in web/src/lib/confirmSilence.ts)
  and renders either the friendly empty state (silenced.length === 0) or the restore list (one row per id with
  a "Restore" button), plus a header "Restore all" when populated. It never touches the network.
- Files:
    feature-views/AdvancedSettings.Model.cs     -- WinUI-free: AdvancedSettingsState enum, AdvancedSettingsRow,
        AdvancedSettingsDisplay, SilencedPromptLabeler (web useSilenceKeyLabel), AdvancedSettingsProjection
        (ordinal dedupe+sort mirroring the web Set + .sort()), AdvancedSettingsRegistration, AdvancedSettingsDiagnostics.
    feature-views/AdvancedSettings.Source.cs    -- WinUI-free: ISilencedPromptsStore seam (P1/S8),
        InMemorySilencedPromptsStore (test/headless), SilencedPromptsStorage (web schema key parity), and the
        pure SilencedPromptsCodec JSON adapter (the web load()/save() bodies; cached document -> projection list).
    feature-views/AdvancedSettings.ViewModel.cs -- WinUI-free state holder; Restore/RestoreAll re-read the store
        (the web handleRestore/handleRestoreAll + setTick re-read), Reload re-resolves labels after a language change.
    feature-views/AdvancedSettings.cs           -- WinUI 3 view (ContentControl): TsFadeIn > TsGlassPanel with a
        cyan accent icon badge (web IconBox/ShieldQuestion) + title/description + header "Restore all", and a body
        that is either TsEmptyState or the restore list; plus the durable LocalSettingsSilencedPromptsStore.
    TeslaSync.App.Tests/FeatureViews/AdvancedSettingsTests.cs -- 46 headless tests (codec adapter, in-memory store,
        labeler, per-state projection, i18n routing, accessibility names, view-model transitions, diagnostics,
        registration, storage-schema parity).
- States: the web source has exactly TWO branches (empty / populated). There is deliberately NO loading / error /
  stale / offline branch -- same precedent as the sibling client-only leaves (JwtDecoder / ToolCard): the read is
  synchronous local storage, and an unreadable store degrades to the empty state (the web load() try/catch -> empty
  set), never a crash or a blank box. Both real branches are reproduced and unit-tested.
- Shared components only: TsGlassPanel, TsButton (ButtonVariant.Subtle/ControlSize.Small = web ghost/sm), TsFadeIn
  (reduce-motion aware), TsEmptyState, DisplayTokens/TypographyTokens, ToolCardAccent. No raw library imports, no
  inline styles, no hardcoded English in the view.
- i18n (all via the P1/S10 ILocalizer facade; English fallback = the web fallback strings; keys already present in
  Strings/{en,he,ar}/Resources.resw under translation.settings.advanced.restoreConfirms.*):
    settings.advanced.restoreConfirms.title / .description / .empty / .restore / .restoreAll
    settings.advanced.restoreConfirms.keys.discardDraft / .keys.unsavedNavigation
  A PrefixLocalizer test proves the projection + labeler feed exactly these catalog keys.
- Accessibility: the surface carries the localized title as its Narrator name; "Restore all" and every per-row
  "Restore" button carry a label-qualified Narrator name; the icon badge is marked AccessibilityView.Raw; the empty
  state is a live region. System font scale + reduce-motion honoured via the shared primitives.
- Telemetry (P1/S11): view.opened slug=AdvancedSettings, PII-safe (never a silenced id), emitted once on Loaded.
